// Repo-local markdownlint config. run-standards.sh prefers this over the
// canonical fleet config when it is present, so anything set here applies to
// CI as well as local runs.
//
// IMPORTANT: a repo-local config REPLACES the canonical one rather than
// extending it, so the `config` block below must mirror
// github-workflows/standards/markdownlint.json. Without it this repo would
// silently pick up rules the fleet has turned off (MD013 line-length being the
// noisy one) and diverge from the standard in ways unrelated to the
// grandfathering this file exists for. If the canonical config changes, this
// block needs the same change.
//
// Why src/content is ignored:
//
// Those files are not hand-authored Markdown. They came from scraping old
// Medium posts, converting to Markdown, and publishing through Astro. The
// conversion left a uniform artifact -- 58 of the 60 findings in this repo were
// MD001 (heading-increment) at line 9 of a content file, where the converter
// emitted an h3 under an h1.
//
// Reflowing the headings of published posts to satisfy a linter would edit
// historical writing to fix a machine-generated artifact, and would change the
// rendered pages. The posts are archival: they are grandfathered, and the
// standard is enforced going forward on everything outside src/content.
//
// This is deliberately a path-scoped ignore rather than disabling MD001
// globally. A new MD001 in docs/ or in a README still fails.
{
  "ignores": ["src/content/**"],
  "config": {
    "default": true,
    "MD013": false,
    "MD024": {
      "siblings_only": true
    },
    "MD029": false,
    "MD033": false,
    "MD036": false,
    "MD040": false,
    "MD046": false,
    "MD060": false
  }
}
